claimed: deploy-cluster -- stage 1 (specs/deployment.md): the `cluster`
target, a Helm chart rendered from the same Deployment value.

Settings become a ConfigMap, a volume becomes a PVC and its mount, a
DNS name with a TLS mode becomes an Ingress, a database becomes a
single-replica StatefulSet that says in the file what it is, and a
neighbour becomes the in-cluster DNS name it already was. Secret
REFERENCES become secretKeyRef entries plus the kubectl command that
creates the Secret -- NOT a templated Secret, which an upgrade would
overwrite with blanks.

Gated by the real tools: `helm lint` and `helm template` on the
rendered chart in the default suite (helm is on this machine and is
pure -- no cluster, no account), kind left Live and optional.

Files: okay-deploy Targets.scala (+ a Cluster renderer), tests,
okay-script's rendered deploy/cluster, specs/deployment.md, boards.
